                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e0a2f0aa-f1e0-393e-8928-e1134e5785ea",
                        "entry_id": "93568b66-0fe5-3eae-8961-602618c12a8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Slipshod; loose and imprecise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "24ffc3f5-457a-4339-a8a3-f6471726525b",
                                "sense_id": "e0a2f0aa-f1e0-393e-8928-e1134e5785ea",
                                "text": "But with how little benefit, the slipslop spelling of proper names and technical terms in official correspondence, and the barbarous names which crowd the face of the best Indian maps, bear witness?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f42e86ae-7ff8-4f0a-a734-22790256d8ac",
                                "sense_id": "e0a2f0aa-f1e0-393e-8928-e1134e5785ea",
                                "text": "It is difficult to ascertain the course of the transaction from the slipslop phrases in which Mr. Gladstone as usual makes the Queen adopt the style of a. literary housemaid; but 'it may be collected that the audacious encroachments of General Butler's contituents and other American fishermen in Canadian waters had exposed their vessels to the risk of legal capture."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0572937a-b1ab-45b0-90d2-687fd800b0f5",
                                "sense_id": "e0a2f0aa-f1e0-393e-8928-e1134e5785ea",
                                "text": "Anything more slipslop than the way in which the inoculations are performed at the Rue d'Ulm it is impossible to imagine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b394c9f-a31a-4b5f-aceb-27e9e828e5a3",
                                "sense_id": "e0a2f0aa-f1e0-393e-8928-e1134e5785ea",
                                "text": "The fact of the matter is that our legislation is constructed in a very slipslop and careless manner."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "586d264c-95eb-3510-90ff-754b6b29c43d",
                        "entry_id": "93568b66-0fe5-3eae-8961-602618c12a8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tending to flop or slide about."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb37b8d0-45ff-4eeb-965d-48865f57da59",
                                "sense_id": "586d264c-95eb-3510-90ff-754b6b29c43d",
                                "text": "All the time this conversation had been going on, we had been scudding along at as brisk a pace as Mouldy's slipslop boots would permit, up the Old Bailey and by Newgate, (where my companions having inquired whether I knew at which door they brought people out to hang 'em, and received from me an intimation that I did not, kindly paused for a moment to enlighten me,) out into Ludgate Street, and across the road into turnings and twistings dingier than any I had yet met with."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2189f51-a4f8-4ec2-a8df-bef5ff3d9627",
                                "sense_id": "586d264c-95eb-3510-90ff-754b6b29c43d",
                                "text": "It dawned on me, in a flash of insight, that slipslop dresses were just a temporary fad and that state of mind was more important than costume ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aac3d8ef-bf51-49f5-ad87-d1795724f88b",
                                "sense_id": "586d264c-95eb-3510-90ff-754b6b29c43d",
                                "text": "An about late forties female in a red G-string swimming bottom with a see-through light yellow beach wrap, stooped to pick a small stone from her slipslop sandals."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                "word": "slipslop",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "84a0638f-f14a-4663-b8ef-e071c4a59c68",
                        "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "slipslops"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec404511-4cf3-357c-ba2a-384ec13576fc",
                        "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nonsense; gibberish; twaddle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a685c1c-011f-4820-8f92-1773fd8a5f20",
                                "sense_id": "ec404511-4cf3-357c-ba2a-384ec13576fc",
                                "text": "... they, consequently, both misconceive and misuse words ; and we are sorry to add, that this childish slipslop, those infantile blunders, is, and are, much more frequently a source of parental mirth, than of parental reprehension : yet it is certain, that such oral deviations, if suffered to continue unremakred, harden into habits, and fix, indelibly fix, the vernacular errors of infancy upon the minds of maturity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1d46a4a-d086-4d8a-ad9e-5a88382a0859",
                                "sense_id": "ec404511-4cf3-357c-ba2a-384ec13576fc",
                                "text": "It is an average specimen of the slipslop and real ignorance generally existing upon the subject."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6d4f42c-b0f4-40f4-b9fa-5fcc89ec5730",
                                "sense_id": "ec404511-4cf3-357c-ba2a-384ec13576fc",
                                "text": "The slipslop which Roman priests, and even the most dignified among the number, are not ashamed to send forth to the world, is something quite inconceivable to those, at least, who have not been nurtured on diet of this kind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46936cd0-5857-402c-9242-38c184060485",
                                "sense_id": "ec404511-4cf3-357c-ba2a-384ec13576fc",
                                "text": "The slipslop which Sir Edward put into the mouth of Mrs. Mivers, the gibberish in which Beck gabbles, may, for all that we know, be totally unlike the language of the back-parlour and of the crossing; and while that doubt continues, the imitation gives us no pleasure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aec573fc-479d-4997-b321-380be6aacc04",
                                "sense_id": "ec404511-4cf3-357c-ba2a-384ec13576fc",
                                "text": "\"So, the modern clergyman still believes in slipslop, does he?\" he exclaimed in his most aggressive manner."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9a1a234-a2a3-307a-80b5-69266459778d",
                        "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Poor writing; text that is imprecise, weak, or overly informal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20b41e1a-a46a-41de-9c9d-02b59aa34833",
                                "sense_id": "a9a1a234-a2a3-307a-80b5-69266459778d",
                                "text": "Imaginary woes, and sentimental slipslop find no responsive chord; but to the historian, the statist, and the geographer, and those who unveil the mysteries of the physical sciences, the field is ever open."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70607c1e-beb6-4c1d-af7f-b95340815b27",
                                "sense_id": "a9a1a234-a2a3-307a-80b5-69266459778d",
                                "text": "No detatched evidence of the slipslop of Mrs. Wood's style (and \" East Lynne \" was in this respect worse, not better, than \" Verner's Pride \") will convey to one who has not read the book itself the impression of ill-written English that every page of her writing gives, even when it contains no technical faults."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d15bd37b-7e43-46dd-8ac8-9162e3c89b41",
                                "sense_id": "a9a1a234-a2a3-307a-80b5-69266459778d",
                                "text": "Plant him in Boston, and his sheet he fills With all the slipslop of his threefold hills, Talks as if Nature kept her choicest smiles Within his radius of a dozen miles, And nations waited till his next Review Had made it plain what Providence must do."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ee2a0f0-698a-49d5-9129-7d2c6ae4ac7e",
                                "sense_id": "a9a1a234-a2a3-307a-80b5-69266459778d",
                                "text": "Nathaniel Hawthorne is, for one, reported to have called him \"a dealer in slipslop on many subjects.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ae820eec-44c6-3f8b-8325-01cce1a9d5eb",
                        "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A quantity of worthless things; mess."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46051ac6-1513-4142-a6c4-1679145e947c",
                                "sense_id": "ae820eec-44c6-3f8b-8325-01cce1a9d5eb",
                                "text": "This story slips for ever through my fingers. I'm very sorry, but I cannot help it; going to sea has given me such a turn for rambling ; besides, I cannot spare the room for all my slipslop."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ab7389d-8e50-41a8-86c3-f207624de554",
                                "sense_id": "ae820eec-44c6-3f8b-8325-01cce1a9d5eb",
                                "text": "Here in our smashing madcap twenty century country all is slipslop and upshot, coming out with moons and planets, down with awful swats at the poors and the darkened. Truly a madcap slipslop, you do well to avoid and to desist from thought of return."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "598da78b-d1a6-4f14-b2f2-799c5f10bc3c",
                                "sense_id": "ae820eec-44c6-3f8b-8325-01cce1a9d5eb",
                                "text": "You wanted no one. I am the slipslop you called for."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "603acdbe-effb-3be9-8c98-f0a277f48670",
                        "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Watery food or drink that is of inferior quality."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6d46897-babc-41ab-a759-2a5f2d17dd5e",
                                "sense_id": "603acdbe-effb-3be9-8c98-f0a277f48670",
                                "text": "They vvere fed very poorly. Once a day they vvould get some slipslop."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab3649bd-40e1-49b4-94f7-528c58fde8a7",
                                "sense_id": "603acdbe-effb-3be9-8c98-f0a277f48670",
                                "text": "'Twas tea time by then, and I fancied a drop Of champagne or cognac—or any slipslop."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3aba0d8-9524-462a-946d-112de39c8850",
                                "sense_id": "603acdbe-effb-3be9-8c98-f0a277f48670",
                                "text": "In your days of leisure, swallow cakes made of broken rice, or cook “slipslop congee”, and hold the bowl between your two hands and eat it with shrugged shoulders."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0b919f97-e09e-35e2-b9d3-d4eddd633aa6",
                        "entry_id": "e256b79a-d9e9-324a-87cb-1a0b90543da1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A splashing, sloshing, or slapping sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "597789c7-2db5-4944-8616-d82d61b83ef0",
                                "sense_id": "0b919f97-e09e-35e2-b9d3-d4eddd633aa6",
                                "text": "The thought drove him forward the more quickly : he paddled strongly with alternate feet and was soon billowing through a regular slipslop of wavelets."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34fc149c-6168-45c1-891f-5f863450c449",
                                "sense_id": "0b919f97-e09e-35e2-b9d3-d4eddd633aa6",
                                "text": "Only then did she hear the slipslop of a familiar footstep coming in through the gate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "178ab9f6-40e2-4131-bd15-5f0008558964",
                                "sense_id": "0b919f97-e09e-35e2-b9d3-d4eddd633aa6",
                                "text": "The rumble of machinery is replaced by the slipslop of the sea against the hull and the splutterings of the VHF."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "907c9516-7040-4f66-b23b-f78a0f8efac1",
                                "sense_id": "0b919f97-e09e-35e2-b9d3-d4eddd633aa6",
                                "text": "Cindy is beside him suddenly, breathing in rhythm with the slipslop of the sea."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
